## 🏛️ Multi-tab architecture (realized)

```
🖥️ main: GitWatcher(worktreePath) → fs.watch(.git/index, .git/HEAD, .git/refs/heads, tree)
           ↓ 200ms debounce
         broadcast → BrowserWindow.getAllWindows().webContents.send('git:diff-changed', {worktreePath})
           ↓ IPC
🪟 renderer: git-diff-store subscribes on first panel, refetches on event
           ↓ single snapshot per (path, params)
         N panels share one fetch / one parse / one tokenize
```

- ❌ Polling not removed — **kept as fallback** (30s when watcher active, 5s otherwise, paused on `document.hidden`)
- 1️⃣ One snapshot per worktree-params key, N subscribers
- ♻️ Parse + tokenize cached globally (LRU 64 / 128 entries)
- 🎁 Tabs on same worktree → near-zero marginal cost

